INT. ALL-NIGHT LAUNDROMAT - 3 A.M.

Fluorescent hum. Dryers turning. A rack of lost socks.

VINNIE CALDERONE (50s, slick hair, silk shirt under a trench coat) sits on a folding table. A gym bag at his feet. He watches a dryer spin.

SHAUNTAE BRIGGS (30s, braids, work boots) folds towels at the counter. Slow. Steady. Eyes on him.

OLEK WISNIEWSKI (20s, hood up, bruise under one eye) feeds quarters into a washer. Misses one. Retrieves it.

A wall phone rings. Everyone stops.

Vinnie crosses. Picks up.

VINNIE
Yeah.

ASANTE (V.O.)
(over phone, flat)
Is it clean?

VINNIE
Clean.

ASANTE (V.O.)
Count it again.

Vinnie covers the receiver. Looks at Shauntae.

VINNIE
(low)
Count it.

SHAUNTAE
Not mine to count.

She folds another towel.

Olek unzips the gym bag. Cash, bundled. He thumbs a stack. Counts under his breath.

OLEK
Forty. Fifty.

ASANTE (V.O.)
Is that Olek I hear?

VINNIE
He's counting.

ASANTE (V.O.)
Tell him it's short by two.

Vinnie stares at the phone. Slowly turns.

VINNIE
(to Olek)
It's short by two.

OLEK
I counted twice.

SHAUNTAE
He's lying.

OLEK
I am not lying.

Vinnie hangs up. Walks toward Olek. Soft shoes on linoleum.

VINNIE
Where's the two?

OLEK
In my pocket. For rent.

SHAUNTAE
Mm-hm.

Vinnie grabs Olek's collar. Slams him into the washer. The drum rattles. Quarters spill.

Shauntae sets down her towel.

SHAUNTAE (CONT'D)
Not here.

VINNIE
Stay out of it.

SHAUNTAE
My sister's laundromat.

The phone rings again. Nobody moves.
